-- title:
--   Power bound for the per-band-triple arithmetic budget
-- statement:
--   Fix $k\in\mathbb N$. Let $R(n)$ be the executable global radix, $P(n)$ the prime-window scale, and $g(n)$ the rounded band size. Define $M(n)=R(n)(4P(n))^2$, $B_k(n)=2(k+2)P(n)^2+1$, and
--   $F_k(n)=10000\bigl(3^{\lceil\log_2 M(n)\rceil}+g(n)B_k(n)+1\bigr)$.
--   Let $E=128H_2(1/256)$, where $H_2$ is binary entropy in bits. For every $\varepsilon>0$, there is $N$ such that
--
--   $$
--   F_k(n)\le n^{\frac85\frac{E+1/2}{5}+\varepsilon}\qquad(n\ge N).
--   $$
--
--   Thus the specified per-triple arithmetic budget has the displayed power bound with arbitrarily small positive slack. This supplies the arithmetic component of the finite resource ledger.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/c0ldzy17/three-sum-lean/blob/2b639655e07421b9ac743de9090459bab473a7c0/Submission/ThreeSum/ArithmeticStageBounds.lean#L127-L143

